<title>UK: BP maintains run cuts at Nerefco refinery - trade.</title>
<headline>BP maintains run cuts at Nerefco refinery - trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum plc (BP) has maintained crude throughput cuts at the Rotterdam refinery it shares with Texaco Netherlands, sources familiar with the refinery said on Friday.</p>
<p>BP, which owns 65 percent of the 400,000 barrel per day (bpd) Pernis and Europoort Nerefco refinery complex, cut crude runs by about 12 percent, equivalent to about 30,000 bpd, on March 6 due to poor margins.</p>
<p>Texaco Netherlands, which controls 35 percent of the complex, returned to full capacity on Thursday having cut crude runs by 12.5 percent -- equivalent to 17,500 bpd -- on March 6.</p>
<p>-- Melanie Goodfellow, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
</text>
